Description: Comprehensive risk assessment toolkit for microbiological 
    dilution testing in food safety. Implements probability estimation and 
    visualization methods using bounded distributions (truncated Poisson and 
    truncated Poisson-lognormal) for both homogeneous and heterogeneous 
    contamination scenarios. Core functionality includes:
    \describe{
      \item{Probability of Detection (PD)}{Estimate the likelihood
        of detecting microbial contamination exceeding specification limits
        under different dilution schemes}
      \item{Probability of Acceptance (PA)}{Evaluate sampling plan
        effectiveness using binomial acceptance probabilities}
      \item{Operating Characteristic (OC) Curves}{Visually compare
        dilution scheme performance across contamination levels}
      \item{Coefficient of Variation (CV)}{Quantify variability in
        microbial concentration estimates}
      \item{True Concentration Estimation}{Back-calculate true
        microbial concentration from observed plate counts}
      \item{Validation Framework}{Compare theoretical and
        simulation-based results to validate risk assessments}
    }
    Designed for food safety professionals, microbiologists, and researchers 
    involved in designing and implementing microbiological monitoring programs 
    and sampling plans compliant with food safety standards.
